.el .ds Aq '
.TH tapectl-init 1  "tapectl-init " 
.SH NAME
tapectl\-init \- Initialize tapectl (DB, config, operator tenant, keys, and the permanent escrow recipient — ADR\-0005; use \-\-no\-escrow to skip it, or \-\-escrow\-public\-key to adopt an existing one instead of minting a new identity)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtapectl init\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-operator\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-escrow\fR] [\fB\-\-escrow\-public\-key\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-home\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Initialize tapectl (DB, config, operator tenant, keys, and the permanent escrow recipient — ADR\-0005; use \-\-no\-escrow to skip it, or \-\-escrow\-public\-key to adopt an existing one instead of minting a new identity)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output in JSON format
.TP
\fB\-\-operator\fR \fI<OPERATOR>\fR
Name of the operator tenant. Defaults to the login name ($USER) — except under a system account (a uid below UID_MIN in /etc/login.defs, such as a `tapectl` service user), where it is required: `init` refuses rather than name the operator after the account
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would be done without making changes. Commands that cannot preview refuse the flag rather than ignore it
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-escrow\fR
Do NOT create the permanent escrow recipient (ADR\-0005) at init. By default `init` generates it and prints its secret once. Use this only when you will adopt an existing escrow identity with `key import \-\-escrow` instead, or in tests/tooling that register escrow separately
.TP
\fB\-\-escrow\-public\-key\fR \fI<KEY_OR_FILE>\fR
Register THIS existing escrow public key (an age1… literal, or a path to a .pub file) instead of minting a new identity — the disaster\-recovery form: a rebuilt machine adopts the original recipient from the heir kit\*(Aqs cover sheet so every tape\*(Aqs receipts keep matching
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Enable verbose output
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip ADR\-0008 Tier\-2 confirmation prompts. It never reaches a Tier\-3 refusal — those are facts, not risks to accept
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<CONFIG>\fR
Path to config file.

NOTE: on its own this ALSO relocates the whole tapectl home to the config file\*(Aqs parent directory — database, keys, staging, receipts. That is how every test harness gets an isolated home, so it still works, but it is surprising enough that it now warns. Use \-\-home when you mean "operate on a different archive", and \-\-config only to point at a config file inside that home.
.TP
\fB\-\-home\fR \fI<HOME>\fR
tapectl home directory: database, keys, catalogs, receipts, logs.

Defaults to ~/.tapectl. The config file is taken from <home>/config.toml unless \-\-config overrides it. Also settable as TAPECTL_HOME.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
